Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:22:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] 3D side by side and top and bottom of a 2160p
 mode go out at 2160p, never at fewer lines

Where the display declares a half 3D layout (side by side or top and
bottom) only at a smaller size than the mode Kodi chose, the output
took the largest such size at the same rate: a 4K video of two views
on a 3840x2160 desktop went out side by side at 1920x1080 60 Hz, each
eye 960x1080, on a TV whose EDID declares 3D only up to 1080p. That
halves each eye again, both ways, while the 2160p mode sends each eye
at 1920x2160.

A half layout now goes out only at a timing of as many lines as Kodi's
mode: at 2160p, told to the display by the mode where the driver lists
that layout at 2160p, else not told, the two halves going out as they
are and the display switched to 3D by hand (as with "Switch the display
to 3D (HDMI)" off). Frame packing is not changed: it exists at 1080p24
and 720p only, keeps each eye whole and still goes to 1080p24 from a
2160p24 mode. Modes of 1080 lines and fewer are chosen as before.

kodi.log now says, with "3D output: the display says that it takes
stereoscopic 3D", at which sizes and rates the driver lists each 3D
layout of the display ("frame packing at 1920x1080@24.000, ...;
side-by-side (half) at 1920x1080@60.000, ..."), or that it lists none
(nvidia-drm, where the half layouts are told by the HDMI vendor
InfoFrame), so that a layout that is not told at a size can be read
from the log.
